WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:06.720
E=mc2 has got to be the most famous equation
in the world. While studying physics. I used

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.889
it countless times and saw it derived in lecture
slides. But I recently realised that I don't

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:18.390
think I've ever read Einstein's original paper
where he derives it for the first time, and

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.439
I'm guessing that you might not have read
it either. But given how ubiquitous the equation

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:28.489
is, doesn't it seem important, or at least
interesting to see its first occurrence in

00:00:28.489 --> 00:00:35.140
the flesh, to read it for ourselves? Well,
here it is. Here's Einstein's paper from 1905,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:41.930
where he first mentions the relationship between
energy and mass. The paper is only three pages

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:46.930
long, and it's not too difficult to understand.
So let's take a look at it. One reason why

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:51.040
you might not have read the original paper
before is because it was written in German.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.490
But math is a universal language, right? So
when I first took a look at it, I was scanning

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:03.810
to see where E=mc2 appeared. And I couldn't
find it. To actually spot it, we need to switch

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:10.009
to the English translation because Einstein
never actually wrote E=mc2 in this paper.

00:01:10.009 --> 00:01:16.889
Instead, he said it in a sentence. If a body
gives off the energy L in the form of radiation,

00:01:16.889 --> 00:01:24.259
its mass diminishes by L over c squared. Rearranging
that sentence, the change in energy L is the

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:30.100
change in mass times the speed of light squared,
we often use E for energy, giving the more

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:38.789
familiar form E=mc2. The equation's message
is that mass and energy are interchangeable.

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:44.569
The title of this paper is, in English, "Does
the inertia of a body depend upon its energy

00:01:44.569 --> 00:01:51.109
content?" we can read inertia as mass here.
It was the fourth paper that Einstein published

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:58.310
in 1905, a year known as his miracle year,
since the four papers revolutionised science's

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:05.320
understanding of the fundamental concepts
of space, time, mass and energy. The other

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:11.500
papers that Einstein published in 1905 were
on the photoelectric effect, Brownian motion

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:17.560
and special relativity. They were all published
in the same journal, the annals of physics.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.261
This one about the mass energy equivalence
wasn't supposed to be a main attraction, it

00:02:22.261 --> 00:02:28.030
was an addition to another paper, just more
of a quick technical note, which is why it's

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:33.740
so short. The paper starts off by saying that
the results of the previous investigation

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:39.310
led to a very interesting conclusion, which
is here to be deduced. Those results he's

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:45.290
referring to are from his recent paper called
On The Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies, which

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:51.460
presented his theory of special relativity.
He summarises a key idea from it, that the

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:57.460
laws of physics must be the same in all non
accelerating reference frames. The first equation

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:03.210
here is one from the Special Relativity paper,
so he doesn't bother deriving it again, but

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:08.240
it is the change in energy of a wave as seen
by a moving observer. It is the relativistic

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:13.750
Doppler effect that he's just discovered in
his previous paper and is excited to explore

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:20.200
what else it can do. L is the energy of the
light wave, c is the speed of light, and v

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.900
is the relative speed between the reference
frames. phi is the angle between the source

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:30.310
and the receiver. The Doppler effect is the
change in frequency of a wave for an observer

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:35.060
who is moving relative to the wave source.
If the source is moving in the direction of

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:40.620
the waves, then those will appear to be more
bunched up and have higher frequency. A common

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:46.600
example of the Doppler shift is when a car
siren approaches you, and you hear a frequency

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:52.930
that is higher than that of the emitted frequency,
and the frequency is lower as it drives away.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:57.690
The relativistic Doppler shift takes into
account the time dilation effects of special

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:04.830
relativity since frequency and energy are
related by E=hf, the energy is also changed

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:10.760
by the same factor. Now that we know how light's
energy changes when viewing it from a moving

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:16.001
reference frame, Einstein then comes up with
a thought experiment for us. Let there be

00:04:16.001 --> 00:04:24.290
a stationary body in the system XYZ, and let
its energy refer to the system XYZ, be E0.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:32.370
Let the energy of the body relative to another
system moving with velocity v, be H0, that

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.770
moving system might be a rocket, let this
body send out in a direction making an angle

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:45.920
phi with the x axis, plane waves of light
of energy half L measured relatively to XYZ

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.240
and simultaneously an equal quantity of light
in the opposite direction. Meanwhile, the

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:57.670
body remains at rest with respect to the system
XYZ, according to the conservation of energy

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:04.020
and the principle of relativity. As we hit
these two equations where E1 and H1 denote

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:09.130
the energy of the body after the emission
of light as measured relative to each of the

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:15.220
two systems. These equations just say that
the energy of the body after emitting light,

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:20.360
plus the energy of the light pulses in each
direction, add to give you what you started

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:25.990
with. That's the conservation of energy. The
same is true for the moving frame of the rocket,

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:31.461
but the light pulses are multiplied by the
relativistic Doppler effect formula. Since

00:05:31.461 --> 00:05:38.450
their energy will appear different to a moving
observer. E0 and H0, both describe the energy

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:45.730
of the same body. In E0, it's from a frame
at rest, and H0, it's from the rocket, the

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:52.600
difference between E0 and H0 will be the kinetic
energy of the body. Remember that according

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:58.419
to the rocket, it's the light emitting body
that seems to be moving at high speed, the

00:05:58.419 --> 00:06:05.440
rocket observer thinks that they are standing
still, H0 minus E0 is the kinetic energy before

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:12.750
the emission of light. And H1 minus E1 is
the kinetic energy after the emission of light.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:19.070
The difference between the two kinetic energies
before and after light emission is this quantity

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:25.790
here, which represents the energy of the light
emitted. Einstein says the kinetic energy

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:30.840
of the body with respect to the moving frame
diminishes as a result of the emission of

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:36.650
light by an amount that is independent of
the properties of the body. Moreover, the

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:43.430
difference in kinetic energy, like the kinetic
energy of the electron depends on the velocity.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:48.720
At this step, Einstein then makes a Taylor
series expansion of this right hand side.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:54.000
That means approximating this function as
a simple polynomial with respect to v over

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.930
c, and centred around zero. And approximation
like this might be helpful because once we

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:05.250
decompose a function into its Taylor series,
we sometimes see terms that are vanishing

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:10.810
in the limit, and can simplify the expression
if we are only interested in finding its limiting

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:18.210
behaviour. For us, the term v over c is so
small that we can neglect magnitudes of fourth

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:26.430
and higher orders to get the change in kinetic
energy is a half times L over c squared times

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:33.590
v squared. Einstein mentioned that this right
hand quantity depended on velocity, just like

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:39.550
the kinetic energy of an electron, which was
known to be a half m v squared. So why not

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:47.250
see if it fits that form? Well, it does if
L over c squared is equal to the mass. So

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:53.710
that's how Einstein concludes If a body gives
off the energy L in the form of radiation,

00:07:53.710 --> 00:08:00.449
its mass diminishes by L over c squared. The
fact that the energy withdrawn from the body

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:06.370
becomes energy of radiation evidently makes
no difference. So that we are led to the more

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:13.050
general conclusion that the mass of a body
is a measure of its energy content is the

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:20.660
energy changes by L. The mass changes in the
same sense by L over the speed of light squared.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:26.900
Finishing off Einstein say something visionary.
It is not impossible that with bodies whose

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:33.260
energy content is variable to a high degree.
For example, with radium salts, the theory

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:39.070
may be successfully put to the test. If the
theory corresponds with the facts, radiation

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:45.520
conveys inertia between the emitting and absorbing
bodies. Einstein was just starting to wrap

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:51.760
his head around the idea that a mass emitting
something massless in the form of light actually

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:57.640
loses mass, and that mass can be transferred
in the form of radiation between emitting

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:02.520
and absorbing the bodies. At first, he didn't
quite believe it, and wrote his friend about

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:08.490
the whole thing saying the principle of relativity
in relation to Maxwell's equations, demands

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:15.450
that mass is a direct measurement of the energy
of a body that light carries mass. A noticeable

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:21.890
decrease in the mass must then occur in the
case of radium. The thought is funny and infectious.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:27.910
But whether God is laughing and has played
a trick on me, I do not know. This relation

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:34.820
between mass and energy has been tied to Einstein's
name and the idea of genius ever since. The

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:40.000
reason that you might not have encountered
the original before could be a general lack

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.820
of emphasis on the history of science alongside
teaching, but it might also be because it

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:52.390
was a bad proof. There are claims that Einstein's
original proof contained circular reasoning,

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:57.820
and there are better ways to derive the same
thing which are more rigorous and more complete.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:04.180
The correctness of Einstein's first proof
is actually a controversy all of its own.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:09.430
Here's a paper published last year summarising
some of the criticisms, including that Einstein's

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:16.060
proof contains circular reasoning, and that
it is only valid to the lowest order approximation

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:21.780
for kinetic energy. Discussion boards online
about this topic are surprisingly heated,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:27.660
bringing in additional factors like the distribution
of credit and fame, amplified by just how

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:33.700
famous this equation has become. What's important
to realise, though, is that the equation itself

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:40.800
is correct. Disputes over the rigour of the
proof are not the same as disputes over the

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:46.640
result. Einstein himself perhaps unsatisfied
with his original proof went on to derive

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:53.250
over a dozen versions of the same result in
later papers, even more proofs of E=mc2 have

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:58.240
been written by others. If you don't like
Einstein's original proof, there are so many

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:03.910
other creative ones to choose from. In a physics
class, it might be more common to derive the

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:11.370
energy momentum relation, which is an extension
of E=mc2 For bodies with some momentum. Without

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:17.560
the first term massless photons would have
no energy. For a body at rest, the first term

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:24.450
disappears and we get E=mc2. And if you're
looking for mathematical rigour, why don't

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:29.780
take a look at Terence Tao's version of the
proof, which follows Einstein steps but in

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:35.020
a more mathematical language then points out
a couple of places where Einstein could have

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:40.260
simplified his proof. Another reason why the
original proof isn't plastered everywhere

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:45.260
might be because of another heated controversy
surrounding it, which has been tearing apart

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:51.950
physics for 100 years. That is the fight over
who deserves credit for relativity, and for

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:52.950
E=mc2.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:58.881
I only just made it up for air after reading
all the criticisms of Einstein's proof. Before

00:11:58.881 --> 00:12:04.279
I fell into the cavern of reading about the
other people who contributed to the idea,

00:12:04.279 --> 00:12:09.029
and how they likely deserve more credit than
they got. Einstein wasn't the first to link

00:12:09.029 --> 00:12:16.270
energy and mass. Even Newton himself pondered
it back in 1717. When he wrote are not the

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:21.970
gross bodies and light convertible into one
another, and may not bodies receive much of

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:27.520
their activity from the particles of light
which enter their composition? Several scientists

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:33.100
working on electromagnetic fields knew that
if a charged body moved through an electromagnetic

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:40.250
field, its mass would be affected. Poincare
in 1900, derived an expression for the conservation

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:48.029
of momentum in electromagnetic systems that
used E=mc2 in calculation although never explicitly

00:12:48.029 --> 00:12:53.500
stated, Einstein seems to have been the first
to establish a mass energy equivalence that

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:59.300
was independent of electromagnetic fields,
and throughout his life, relentlessly devoted

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:07.080
time and effort to establishing E=mc2 as a
universal law applicable to all forms of matter

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:13.250
and energy. So in this sense, it does seem
justified to associate the idea with Einstein,

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:18.730
that association would come as a curse when
the public started to link the equation with

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:27.149
nuclear weapons. After the bombings of Hiroshima
and Nagasaki in 1945, 40 years after Einstein's

00:13:27.149 --> 00:13:34.990
paper, E=mc2 was featured in the Smith report,
the official US government release about the

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:42.150
development of the atomic bomb. E=mc2 can
be used to quantify the amount of energy released

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:48.459
or consumed by nuclear reactions, which convert
mass into energy. If you measure the mass

00:13:48.459 --> 00:13:53.390
of all the constituents and the mass of all
the products, and multiply the difference

00:13:53.390 --> 00:14:00.019
by c squared, you get how much energy is released
or consumed, usually in the form of light

00:14:00.019 --> 00:14:06.010
and heat. With c squared being such a large
number, you can see that an extraordinarily

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:11.900
large amount of energy can be released from
just a small amount of mass millions of times

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:19.040
more so than in the combustion of chemical
explosives. Whilst E=mc2 is useful for quantifying

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:23.630
the amount of energy released, it was not
strictly necessary for the development of

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:30.070
the atomic bomb, especially since the fission
process was known in 1938. It surprised me

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:37.130
to learn that the neutron wasn't discovered
until 1932, 27 years after Einstein's paper

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:42.550
and a much more crucial discovery to the development
of the weapon. Einstein himself co signed

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:49.110
a letter to the US president in 1939, urging
funding into research for Atomic Energy, warning

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:56.089
that an atomic bomb was theoretically possible.
He would later come to regret that letter.

00:14:56.089 --> 00:15:01.279
Newton please forgive me, he would write,
not referring directly to the bomb, but for

00:15:01.279 --> 00:15:06.519
standing on Newton's shoulders, for taking
his work and questioning its foundations,

00:15:06.519 --> 00:15:14.410
flipping it, building upon it and driving
progress to both the good and bad consequences.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:19.700
The mention of war in the story reminds us
how often scientific discoveries are tied

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:26.769
to both amazing and sometimes terrible consequences.
Much of the technology which has improved

